# The transform, restated in VRL. One decoded SensorBatch in, up to 100 rows out.
#
# Assigning an array to `.` makes remap emit one event per element, with
# acknowledgement state shared across the children, so the source's offset
# commits only once ClickHouse has acked every row derived from the message.
#
# The constants are restated here rather than imported: `methodology/` makes the
# flatten, the filters and the derived columns user code in every system, and
# `harness/tests/each_arm_restates_the_transform.rs` holds the two below to
# `workload/workload.toml`. It matches by substring over the whole file, so no
# comment here may spell either needle.

batch_id = int!(.batch_id)
sensor   = string!(.sensor)

# `region` is a nullable Avro union; the column is LowCardinality(String), not
# Nullable.
region = .region
region = if region == null { "" } else { string!(region) }

batch_ts = from_unix_timestamp!(int!(.batch_ts_ms), unit: "milliseconds")
send_ts  = from_unix_timestamp!(int!(.send_ts_us),  unit: "microseconds")

# `del` rather than a plain read throughout: VRL clones the whole variable to
# read one field off it, and clones an array again on assignment
# (vectordotdev/vector#6770). `del(.events)` moves the array off the event, and
# `del(e.field)` reads without copying the record. Mutating the closure's local
# is invisible — its return value replaces the element.
#
# `recursive: false` is load-bearing: rows legitimately carry a null `quality`
# and an empty `tags`, which a recursive compact would strip. Only the
# top-level nulls, the filtered-out rows, may go.
#
# `q == null ||` short-circuits before the fallible coercion, so a null quality
# is never coerced.
#
# f64 is exact for value_scaled: the numerator is below 2^41 and the divisor at
# most 100, so `to_int` truncates toward zero as specified. `?? 0.0` only arms
# the type checker's divide-by-zero case, unreachable since seq >= 0.
#
# `upcase` is Unicode, equal to ASCII uppercase on this corpus's fixed set of
# lowercase ASCII metric names; the gate's checksum over name_upper catches it
# if that stops being true.
. = compact(map_values(array!(del(.events))) -> |e| {
    q = del(e.quality)
    u = string!(del(e.unit))
    if u != "drop" && (q == null || float!(q) >= 0.2) {
        seq   = int!(del(e.seq))
        value = int!(del(e.value))
        scaled = to_int(value * 1000 / (seq + 1) ?? 0.0)
        {
            "batch_id": batch_id, "event_seq": seq, "sensor": sensor, "region": region,
            "name_upper": upcase(string!(del(e.name))), "unit": u,
            "value": value, "value_scaled": scaled, "quality": q, "tags": del(e.tags),
            "batch_ts": batch_ts, "send_ts": send_ts
        }
    } else {
        null
    }
}, recursive: false)
